// @generated from the GNU Emacs 30.2 Darwin oracle: every name that a
// `DEFVAR_LISP', `DEFVAR_LISP_NOPRO', `DEFVAR_BOOL', `DEFVAR_INT',
// `DEFVAR_PER_BUFFER' or `DEFVAR_KBOARD' across src/*.c declares AND that
// the pinned oracle binary actually forwards at `-Q --batch'.  A name whose
// defining file is not compiled into this build (android, w32, haiku,
// pgtk, dbus, ...) or that sits under an `#ifdef' the build does not take
// is a plain symbol there and is left out.  The probe is
// eval.c:Fdefvaralias itself, which refuses to alias a `SYMBOL_FORWARDED'
// symbol ("Cannot make a built-in variable an alias") and a forwarded
// symbol that C or Lisp has since made `SYMBOL_LOCALIZED' ("Don't know how
// to make a buffer-local variable an alias"); both carry a C slot.  The
// second list is the subset the oracle reports as already localized at
// `-Q --batch' (buffer.c and keyboard.c call Fmake_variable_buffer_local
// on them during initialization).  The mandatory anti-cheat gate
// regenerates both lists against the pinned oracle and requires byte
// identity.  Sorted and deduplicated.

